WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.575
A word on the numbers themselves, because the format trips people up.

2
00:00:04.825 --> 00:00:07.150
One degree is sixty minutes.

3
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.050
Not a hundred.

4
00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:13.250
The training chart’s scales divide each minute into tenths.

5
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:17.875
So a position reads in degrees, minutes, and tenths of a minute.

6
00:00:18.125 --> 00:00:23.100
Forty-one degrees, eighteen point five minutes means eighteen and a half minutes.

7
00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:27.575
Don’t confuse that with the older format of minutes and seconds.

8
00:00:27.825 --> 00:00:32.200
Eighteen point five minutes is eighteen minutes and how many seconds?

9
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.625
Thirty.

10
00:00:34.875 --> 00:00:36.425
Half a minute.

11
00:00:36.675 --> 00:00:38.350
Not fifty.

12
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.450
Count the small tick marks carefully, too.

13
00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:46.025
The scale isn’t always divided the same way all over the chart.

14
00:00:46.275 --> 00:00:52.225
And always write latitude first, with north or south, then longitude, with east or west.
